package mapdemo

// A map whose VALUE is a TEXT BUFFER (docs/SPEC-TABLES.md §2.5, §2.8): "A VALUE
// is anything a table field can hold ... `*string` (§2.5)". A buffer is a NODE,
// so the value is an ordinary pointer field of the generated entry and its
// storage is that field's own row, the eight-byte reference (§4.2). The handle
// is that SLOT, which is what an Emplace fills, and two keys may name one
// buffer exactly as two pointer fields may.

table Docs
{
    pages map[string(8)]*string // *string: a text buffer at its used size
    after int32
}
